<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  DAR-BE-318 plan 3b-1 (ruling P3b1-9). What the Shopify endpoints do that darpan core must know without naming Shopify: set
  here, on the core connector rows by primary key (the other fields stay core's), never in core.

  excludedRecordsSidecar: whether the records Keep sets aside are written beside the extract (the excluded-records side
  file). No Shopify extract filters at the read since DAR-BE-318 plan 3b-2b (Tasks 21-23): darpan's Spark Keep writes it
  when this says Y, and a kept-copy slice exactly when this says Y.
    SHOPIFY Y, SHOPIFY_ORDER_LINE_UNITS Y: Spark Keep writes the side file for the orders and line-unit extracts.
    SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS N: its read never wrote one, so a run that sets events aside reads them as unknown, as before.

  keepLinesJson []: Shopify declares no built-in Keep line; the extracts drop nothing of their own that a rule could name
    (zero-quantity and orphan lines, a return that has a refund, a closed unrefunded return stay in the extractor). A
    Spark-placed connector row carries an explicit value, so a row that lost its line is never taken for one that has none.

  servingProjectionServiceName: SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS names project#ShopifyReturnRefsKeptRecords, which refuses every side (the
    live read adds a 3 h lookback a slice cannot), so even a connector flag flipped to keep instants never serves a copy.

  datasetReadParametersJson: sent on every dataset read of the endpoint (a rolling copy of its events).
    SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS {"preserveWindowInstants":true,"lookbackHours":0}: a run read rounds its window to whole days in the
      store's zone and widens it back by lookbackHours (3, for the OMS sync lag), so the connector row cannot keep its instants
      (that would change every tenant's live read). The copy's read keeps the instants and the lookback off, so it holds
      exactly the events created in its rolling window. A run side is therefore never cut from it (its live window is the
      rounded, widened one) and reads live; see ShopifyReturnRefsRollingCopyTests.
-->
<entity-facade-xml type="darpan-seed">
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector systemEnumId="SHOPIFY" excludedRecordsSidecar="Y" keepLinesJson="[]"/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_ORDER_LINE_UNITS" excludedRecordsSidecar="Y" keepLinesJson="[]"/>
    <darpan.reconciliation.SourceSystemConnector systemEnumId="SHOPIFY_RETURN_REFS" excludedRecordsSidecar="N" keepLinesJson="[]"
            servingProjectionServiceName="reconciliation.ShopifyOrderExtractionServices.project#ShopifyReturnRefsKeptRecords"
            datasetReadParametersJson='{"preserveWindowInstants":true,"lookbackHours":0}'/>
</entity-facade-xml>
